 **Not checked in the running game** -- worth a Heroic Silence the Loom
 clear and a look in the Wardrobe.
+
+### Champion: per-class Champion skins (patch 0435)
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Champion
+
+- Added Champion, a sixth skin set for every hero class: your heroes in their own colours, upgraded with crowns, gold-trimmed plate, longer capes and proper padding
+- Added a headband with trailing ribbons for the Samurai, new capes for the Huge Knight, Gladiator, Minotaur, Werewolf, Lizardman, Kobold and Wizard, and barding for the Centaur's horse
+- Added Champion unlocks: clear The Siege of Blackford Keep on Heroic or harder with a hero in the party to earn that class's Champion, then unlock it for 5,000 gold
+- Champion is listed first in the Wardrobe's sets, since it's the earliest one to earn
+```
+
+Direct request: the last planned set, from a ChatGPT knight mockup that
+keeps the default palette but reads as an *upgraded* knight (gold crown
+with a red gem, gold-trimmed plate, bigger plume, longer flowing cape,
+silver shield with a red star). Brief: "added padding on unarmoured
+areas, longer capes, etc; a headband for the samurai (think Kiriko)".
+Decisions locked in conversation: name **Champion**, tied to **The
+Siege of Blackford Keep on Heroic or harder** (lvl 8 -- the one raid
+without a set, and makes this the early-game set the tints were
+standing in for), **5,000 gold per class**, no Steam achievement. idle +
+walk (+ run for the knight) only.
+
+**Data-only.** One new skins.json entry, `champion` (cost 5000, swatch
+`#ffc825`/`#c42430`, `perClass: true`, `unlockRaidId:
+"blackford_keep"`, `unlockMinDifficulty: "heroic"`), inserted *before*
+`frost_sovereign` so it's the first set the Wardrobe lists -- it's the
+earliest to earn (lvl 8). The rest keep their existing order (Frost
+Sovereign 18, Bound Wraith 22, Paladin 41, Demonic 26, Void 43); swap
+Paladin and Demonic in skins.json if you want strict unlock order.
+No code changes.
+
+**Art (not in git):** `public/heroes/<class>/champion/{idle,walk}.png`
+for all 14 classes + `knight/champion/run.png` -- 29 sheets, same sizes
+as `original/`, already in the local copy. No palette changes; every
+upgrade is a shape added in the class's own colours plus the packs'
+shared gold and reds.
+
+Per class:
+- **Knight** (the mockup): plume grown out through its own outline,
+  gold crown with a glinting red gem, gold rims on helm and pauldrons,
+  cape lengthened to the ground with a gold hem, silver shield with a
+  gold rim and red star.
+- **Huge Knight**: five-point crown, gold rims, fuller plume, new red
+  cape behind.
+- **Adventurer**: gold-rimmed gauntlets, cloak lengthened, small
+  pauldron.
+- **Gladiator**: gold-rimmed helm, padded upper arm, short red cape.
+- **Samurai**: Kiriko-style red headband across the forehead, knotted
+  at the back, two thin ribbons (one drooping) trailing behind with
+  white tips, waving on a loop; gold-edged collar.
+- **Witch**: gold circlet on the hood, gold-edged robe.
+- **Pyromancer**: gold-edged hood, gold-rimmed gauntlet, pauldron,
+  longer robe.
+- **Wizard**: long blue cape, longer beard.
+- **Dwarf**: crown on the helm, gold rims, longer cape.
+- **Kobold**: pauldron, red cape.
+- **Lizardman**: quilted red gambeson over the belly with a gold edge,
+  pauldron, red cape.
+- **Minotaur**: gold horn tips, studded chest strap, pauldron, red cape.
+- **Werewolf**: pauldron, red cape hung from the top of its back (so it
+  sits behind the body in the crawling walk instead of under it).
+- **Centaur**: quilted red barding with a gold edge across the horse's
+  back, pauldron.
+
+**Generator in the repo:** `tools/skin-gen/champion/` (`run.py`,
+`asc.py`, `aclasses.py`); reuses `tools/skin-gen/paladin/`. Verified it
+reproduces the shipped sheets byte-for-byte.
+
+**Backlog update:** Blackford Keep now has a set, so if the tints are
+retired later (see 0434), Champion is the early-game replacement.
+Requiem for the Last God is the only raid still without one.
+
+**Not checked in the running game** -- worth a Heroic Blackford Keep
+clear and a look at the Wardrobe order.
